<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Kairos posts 42.8 mln rand 15 month loss.</title>
<headline>Kairos posts 42.8 mln rand 15 month loss.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>15 months ended Sept 30 versus year ended June 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Loss per shr (cts)    N/A	   vs  19.6</p>
<p>    Attrib loss	     42.83	 vs  28.75</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   42.97	 vs  29.43</p>
<p>    Tax			  0.05	 vs    -</p>
<p>    Finance costs	    8.7	  vs  14.33</p>
<p>    Turnover		 155.58	 vs 299.74</p>
<p>Full name: Kairos Industrial Holdings</p>
<p>NOTE - The group said that as a result of its restructuring and recapitalisation it was well focused on its three core businesses and management was satisfied that it had resolved the problems of the underperforming businesses either through disposal or reorganisation.</p>
<p>It said that prospects for its organic growth and growth through targeted acquisitions were good and management expected the disposal of the loss-making oeprations to achieve acceptable earnings for the year ending September 30, 1997.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
